{{/*
  beads-issues/shared/loop-driver-guidelines-parallel — the 3 "## Guidelines"
  bullets used only by the parallel-fanout loop drivers (loop-fixing-bug,
  loop-implementing-feature): One phase per run / Parallelize only when
  genuinely independent / Never do the phase work inline. Publish-post is
  a label-only driver (no per-phase send_prompt fan-out) and does NOT use
  this fragment.

  Callers pass the phase-chain, split-antipattern noun, and per-phase
  label list to splice into the bullet text:

      {{ template "beads-issues/shared/loop-driver-guidelines-parallel" (dict
          "Chain"            "`researched` → `reproduced` → `fixed`"
          "SplitAntipattern" "a single-root-cause fix or work that shares files"
          "LabelList"        "`researched`/`reproduced`/`fixed`"
      ) }}

  Parameters:
    Chain            — the ordered phase chain as it appears in the
                       "One phase per run" bullet (backtick-quoted labels
                       joined by ` → `).
    SplitAntipattern — noun phrase spliced after "never split " in the
                       "Parallelize only when genuinely independent" bullet.
    LabelList        — slash-joined per-phase labels spliced into the
                       "Never do the phase work inline" bullet after
                       "`bd update ... --add-label` for ".

  The output is column-0 text (matches the existing beads-issues/shared/*
  fragments' convention). The caller's YAML `content: |` scalar's own
  indentation is applied by the YAML loader before the template engine
  runs, so this fragment renders at the same visible indent as the
  caller's surrounding bullets — no double-indentation.
*/ -}}
- **One phase per run.** Dispatch a single phase prompt ({{ .Chain }}) via
  `mitto_conversation_send_prompt`, then end the turn. Never skip a stage or dispatch
  two at once. The sole exception is **Step 3f (Parallel fan-out)**, which resolves
  one genuinely decomposable stage across parallel children within a single run.
- **Parallelize only when genuinely independent.** Prefer the single self-send phase by
  default. Only fan out (Step 3f) when the stage's work splits into disjoint,
  non-conflicting parts with no interdependencies and children can be spawned; never
  split {{ .SplitAntipattern }}.
- **Never do the phase work inline.** The whole point of this driver is per-phase
  model tiering. If you catch yourself running `bd update ... --add-label` for
  {{ .LabelList }} inside *this* prompt, stop — that is the phase prompt's job. This
  driver only labels `needs-human` (Step 4) and closes on Done. The one documented
  exception is **Step 3f**: when a stage is distributed across parallel children,
  this driver adds that stage's label itself after synthesizing and verifying the
  children's reports.